  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ee2cfa6a-5766-506c-b6df-219fb2b6b845" activityNameId="05fff6ab-a3f9-5656-ac06-52334c4ad260" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Chlorine, gaseous, diaphragm cell, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Chlorine, gaseous, diaphragm cell, at plant
The multioutput-process "chlor-alkali electrolysis, diaphragm cell" delivers the co-products "chlorine, gaseous, diaphragm cell, at plant", "sodium hydroxide, 50% in water, diaphragm cell, at plant" and "hydrogen, liquid, diaphragm cell, at plant". The allocation is done according to the masses of the different products - i.e. 46.4% chlorine - 52.3% sodium hydroxide and 1.3% hydrogen.;
UUID: 527bc704-38dc-3061-b093-371023213c49
Besides the electrolysis process in a diaphragm cell, the following process steps are included into this process: brine production, brine purification, brine resaturation as well as the final handling of the electrolysis products, without the chlorine liquifaction!
Location: European average values
Technology: present state of technology used in european diaphragm cells
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Average values from the ranges indicated in EC IPPC-BAT document are used 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_527bc704-38dc-3061-b093-371023213c49.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
